--- text
█▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀█
█ Add Comment                                                                                                                                                  █
█ ▎ +Run `viewer FILE`, then press `j` and `k` to move.                                                                                                        █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  Write   Preview  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── █
█  Mention the arrow keys too.                                                                                                                                 █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  The README's Keys section should say what this line does in a little more detail. Here's what I'd add:                                                      █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  • j / k move one line and stop at either end of the file; they never wrap around.                                                                           █
█  • G jumps to the last line and g to the first.                                                                                                              █
█  • J / K move by hunk, and stop at the first and the last hunk.                                                                                              █
█  • The arrow keys do the same as j and k, and page up and page down move by a screen.                                                                        █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  I checked each of these against the current build and they all behave as described, so this is only a docs change. If you want, I can open a follow-up for  █
█  wrapping around at the ends, but I'd keep it behind a setting so the default stays the same as today.                                                       █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  The help panel lists j as "Line down" but the footer says "Down". We should pick one; I'd go with the help panel's wording because it's more specific.      █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  Steps I ran:                                                                                                                                                █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█   1. Open a file longer than the screen                                                                                                                      █
█   2. Press G                                                                                                                                                 █
█   3. Press j, then k, then g                                                                                                                                 █
█   4. Press J and K on a file with three hunks                                                                                                                █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  Every one of them stopped where the docs will say it stops. The only surprise was K on the first hunk, which does nothing rather than wrapping to the last  █
█  one, and that matches the rest.                                                                                                                             █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  The screenshot in the README is from 0.5 and still shows the old title bar. It'd be worth refreshing it in the same PR.                                     █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  A few notes for whoever picks up the wrap-around follow-up:                                                                                                 █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  • keep the default as it is today                                                                                                                           █
█  • put the setting next to the other viewer settings                                                                                                         █
█  • make G and g respect it too, so the keys stay consistent                                                                                                  █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█  That's all from me on this line.                                                                                                                            █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
█                                                                                                                                                              █
